1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Albert_de_Longueval,_Count_of_Bucquoy '''Charles Albert de Longueval, III, comte de Bucquoy '''] - Wikipedia - English (car)
2 CONT * '''born''' - 1607
2 CONT * '''died''' - 29 March 1663
2 CONT * '''son of''' - Charles Bonaventura de Longueval and Maria Magdalena, comtesse de Biglia
2 CONT * '''married''' - Maria Wilhelmine de Croÿ Solre
2 CONT * '''children''' - The couple had 13 children
2 CONT * He was a military commander, holder of high office, and nobleman in the Habsburg realms of the Low Countries and Bohemia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT * His lordships included Buquoy, Achiet-le-Petit, Puisieux, Gratzen, Rosenberg, Libiegitz, and Farciennes.  He had the castel of Farciennes built in 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT * His military and civil offices included hereditary Master of the Hunt of Artois (1631-1659), captain general, grand bailiff and sovereign governor of the County of Hainaut, governor of Valenciennes, general of artillery, and gen
2 CONC eral of the Spanish cavalry in the Low Countries.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was a '''knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece''' (invested Vienna, 1650) and a commander in the '''Order of Calatrava'''.
