1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles-Pierre de Villeneuve, nobleman of Saint-Laurent, born and baptized March 26, 1724, at Valensole (r.p.), was second lieutenant in regiment of Flandre infantry July 28, 1742. Attendant of the battle of Coni, 
2 CONC in 1744; named lieutenant of the same regiment January 11, 1744. Captain of the same regiment September 1, 1748 and knight of Sainte-Louis in 1760, he discharged the service in 1761. His inheritance, in 1760, of a part of the lord
2 CONC ship of Saint-Laurent, of which he bequeathed to Augustin Serre, spouse of Marie-Aimare de Villeneuve-Cananilles (p. 205) and was sold to Charles-Alexandre de Mazenod.  He testifird October 13, 1780 (pr.) in favor of his son, Silv
2 CONC estre, made legacies for his other children and for his brothers and sisters, bequeathed the ___(?) profit of his goods to his wife and died June 9, 1781, at Valensole (r.p.).
