1 NAME Gabrielle /de Barjon/
2 GIVN Gabrielle
2 SURN de Barjon
2 _MARNM Bondurant
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 18 JAN 1643
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint-Étienne-Vallée-Française
3 STAE Occitanie
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 MAR 1695
2 PLAC Génolhac, Gard, Languedoc-Roussillon
2 ADDR
3 CTRY France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The record of baptism of Gabrielle de Barjon, wife of Jean Pierre Bondurant, Sieur de Cougoussat, show that she was born 18 January 1643, at St. Etienne, Ville francaise (Lozere), and was the daughter of the Minist
2 CONC er Pierre Barjon, Minister of that place, and Jeanne de Belcastle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Register of Baptisms, Marriages and Burials of the Reformed Church of Barre des Cevennes
2 CONT
2 CONT "Tuesday morning, 28 October 1676, by me, the undersigned Minister, marriage was solemnized in the Church of Barre, between Jean Pierre Bondurant, Sieur de Cougoussat, bourgoise inhabitant of the village of Genolhac, age 40 years,
2 CONC  and demoiselle Gabrielle Barjon, age 34 years, inhabitant of Barre" signed: Guillaume Barjon, Minister
2 CONT
2 CONT (Guillaume Barjon was the brother of Gabrielle de Barjon)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Gabrielle de Barjon and Jean Pierre Bondurant are:
2 CONT * +Jean Pierre Bondurant, b. July 12, 1677, Genolhac, France, d. Abt. 1734, Goochland County, VA.
2 CONT * Francoise Bondurant, b. April 12, 1681, d. date unknown, Baptised Protestant.
2 CONT * Jean Pierre Bondurant, b. December 04, 1684, d. date unknown, Baptised Catholic.
2 CONT
2 CONT [NOTE from Curator: are these two different sons named Jean Pierre? This needs to be resolved from the records.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/e/p/l/John-W-Epling/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0557.html for this information.
