1 NOTE ****NOTES ;
2 CONT         LAND, September 17, 1731 Thomas Tanner Jr. bought 200 acres in Goochland Co on the south side of the James River adjoining Matthew Agee and John Peter ( Jean Pierre) Bondurant .
2 CONT         OTHER SOURCES ; Will dated September 05, 1734 probate. Jan. 21, 1735.
2 CONT
2 CONT         LAND, September 17, 1731 Thomas Tanner Jr. bought 200 acres inGoochland Co on the south side of the James River adjoining Matthew Ageeand John Peter ( Jean Pierre) Bondurant .
2 CONT         OTHER SOURCES ; Will dated September 05, 1734 probate. Jan. 21,1735.
2 CONT                                          See pg. 107, Vol 33, May 02.1995 Magazine of Va. Genealogy .
2 CONT                                          His name is listed on Tithable List , Goochland County , Va.
2 CONT                                          August 1723 there is a case in Henrico Court Order Book involving Richard Ward Jr. vs John Peter Bondurant
2 CONT
2 CONT **** Jean Pierre fled France and arrived in Aarau, Switzerland in Feb, 1697 where he joined his maternal uncle Guillaume Barjon . Pastor of the Huguenot refugee Church there . In 1699, in the company of Pastor Barjon and other ref
2 CONC ugees , he went to Karshafen , Germany . There is no record of his travel from Karshafen to England , but he was among the Huguenot refugees arriving at the mouth of the James River in Virginia on Sept. 20 , 1700 abroad the ship "
2 CONC  Ye Peter and Anthony " , which had sailed from England .
2 CONT Jean Pierre's grandfather Pierre Bondurant was a Doctor of Law and was apparently successful . His Father Jean Pierre Sr. , Sieur de Cougoussat Advocate , did not seem to be as successful as he wasin debt when he died. At one time
2 CONC  Jean Pierre JR , the immigrant was forced to accept public assitance from the Church of Rome . He was apprenticed to his father's cousin Andre , A Master Apothecary . where Jean Pierre Jr. learned enough medicine to be accounted 
2 CONC asa Doctore in the Colonies of Virginia .
2 CONT
2 CONT *** He was listed as a " fugitive from the Kingdom because of religion " in 1712 . This late date is not significant , as such listings were normally late ; and his father's cousin was Consul General of the listings.
2 CONT
2 CONT ****NOTES ;
