2 NOTE "September 14, 1759 - Seven Years War - The Marquis de Montcalm dies of wounds at 5 am the morning after the Battle of the Plains of Abraham, at age 47. When informed he is dying, Montcalm supposedly replied, So much the better. I
3 CONC  shall not live to see the English masters of Québec. An elderly servant nicknamed Bonhomme Michel fashions a makeshift coffin out of a few boards. At 9:00 that evening, the general's body, preceded by a soldier carrying a cross a
3 CONC nd two militia men lighting the way with lanterns, is borne quietly down Rue Saint-Louis to the chapel of the Ursuline convent. The procession turns left onto Rue du Parloir, a tiny street dominated by the convent. After a funeral
3 CONC  mass, Montcalm's body is laid in a crater that a British shell had carved out under the altar. Bonhomme Michel then repairs the floor as best he can. Quebec, Quebec" Jacques Paquin on Facebook Sept 15, 2017
