1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Félicité Perpétue Catherine Liardet (born de Paul de Lamanon D'Albe)
2 CONT FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT Birth:	Sep 1768 - Salon-de-Provence, Bouches-du-Rhône, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France
2 CONT Death:	July 20 1845 - Regents Park, London, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT Parents:	Duc Andre Auguste de Paul de Lamanon D'Albe, Elizabeth D'Albe (born de Requiston d'Hauteville)
2 CONT Husband: John Robert James William Tell Liardet
2 CONT Children:	William Liardet, Anastasia Giovanni De Liardet, Perpetue Felicite Heydon (born De Liardet), Francis Liardet, Louisa Félicité Liardet, Caroline Frederica Evelyn Liardet (born Liardet)
2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT Updated 21st June 2023: Notes by W. J.E.W.. 
2 CONT '''YET TO IDENTIFY a 5th child shown: Anastasia Giovanni Liardet - I cannot IDENTIFY this Profile as being legitimate''' Profiles Added by Ange on December 31, 2008 and Managed by: Erin Ishimoticha
2 CONT '''Countess Félicité-Perpétue Catherine (nee Paul de Lamanon D'Albe 11), Liardet:'''
2 CONT AKA: Félicité Paul de Lamanon, AND Félicité-Perpétue Catherine de Paul de Lamanon D'Albe, was born at Salon Bouches-du-Rhone, Provence-Alpes-Coter d'Azur, France. Educated at the Royal Convent School of Saint-Cyr, Paris, Île-de-Fr
2 CONC ance. Aka: Perpétue, became 'Lady in Waiting' to Marie Antoinette. Escaping France & the revolution, she married in Hamburg, Germany - her brother, Pierre Paul de Lamanon D'Albe (Prebendary of the Church of Aix) at her side - who 
2 CONC later met his fate with the Guillotine. Félicité-Perpétue was aged 26 years, 7 years older than her husband, Major John Robert James William Guillaume Tell Liardet [19-20 years], whom she married on 4 February 1794. Liardet was a 
2 CONC Major of the Royal British Navy, legate to Spain & Employed by the Swiss Guard. The young couple made their home in London, where '''4 children were born to them'''. Liardet called her Félicité. He died 10 years later in Gibraltar
2 CONC  of yellow fever in 1804, aged 29. Félicité-Perpétue was then 36. Félicité married her 2nd husband Charles William Heydon 4 years later on November 17th 1808. She died aged 77 after 30 years of widowhood. 
2 CONT Félicité-Perpétue was the daughter of the Noble Duke Andre Auguste de Paul de Lamanon d'Albe & Lady Elizabeth de' Requiston d'Hauteville. Another Profiler established that Félicité-Perpétue was also a wife of Charles William Heydo
2 CONC n. Charles would have died around 1815 as records show that Félicité died aged 77 after 30 years of widowhood. Date of 2nd Marriage to Charles William Heydon now verified.
2 CONT
2 CONT Félicité-Perpétue's ancestry can easily be traced to the foundations of Rome, Alba Long & the Patriarchs of (Napoli) Naples. The Surname d'Albe (French) Alba (Italian) Alva (Spanish) is known in many royal households, especially t
2 CONC he Maison de Bourbon as she was not only a "Lady In Waiting" for Queen Marie Antoinette, but also cousin to King Louis XV1 de'Bourbon of France. Félicité was also known as: La Comtesse Perpétue Catherine de Paul de Lamanon D'Albe.
2 CONC
2 CONT Countess Félicité-Perpétue Catherine Liardet had Four children to Liardet:
2 CONT 1. Francis Liardet - Cpt.(1783-1863),
2 CONT 2. William Liardet - (1794-18?),
2 CONT 3. Louisa Felicia Maria (1799-1875) (who married John Faithful Fortescue Wright (1786-1853) and Dr Charles Henry Moffitt), and
2 CONT 4. Carolina Frederica Liardet (1803-1882).
2 CONT '''5.''' This 5th child shown as: Anastasia Giovanni Liardet - cannot be identified in family records as being legitimate. The Profile was dded by Ange on December 31, 2008 and Managed by: Erin Ishimoticha - However, the child's d
2 CONC ate of Birth is given as September 29th 1794 & died perhaps 4 weeks later, as a baby, in Novemb3r 1794.
1 NOTE {geni:hair_color} Brown
1 NOTE {geni:eye_color} Brown
