1 NAME John Peter /Bondurant/ I
2 GIVN John Peter
2 SURN Bondurant
2 NSFX I
2 _MARNM Bondurant
2 NICK John Peter Bondurant
1 NAME Jean-Pierre /Bondurant/ Jr.
2 GIVN Jean-Pierre
2 SURN Bondurant
2 NSFX Jr.
2 _MARNM Bondurant
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 OCT 1709
2 ADDR
3 CITY Manakin
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1774
2 PLAC King William Parish, Goochland,Virginia, United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JOHN PETER BONDURANT, the second, son of Dr. John Peter and
2 CONT Ann Bondurant, married Sarah Moseley, widow of Robert L. Moseley, in 1729. In a 1748 record, John Peter Bondurant was listed as a vestryman in King William Parish. In 1734 John's name was the first mentioned in his father's will. 
2 CONC John Peter and his wife Sarah lived in Goochland County, Virginia and later in Cumberland County. On March 9, 1758, he deeded his son, John Peter the third, of Albemarle County, 200 acres of land. After county lines changed, this 
2 CONC was in Buckingham County. The names of members of the family of John are found frequently in early court and Church records. Recorded, also, are many land grants from Royal Governors to the Bondurants. Here began a lineage of Bond
2 CONC urants who became prominent citizens in Buckingham County and today includes many of distinction, scattered all over the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peter Bondurant, the second, and Sarah Rachel Mosely had four sons. They were:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN BONDURANT III, son of John, II, and Sarah Moseley Bondur-
2 CONT ant born in 1737 in Manakin Town. Died in Adairlo County, 1807.
2 CONT married Martha Allen, daughter of David and Martha Allen.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, III, was the forerunner of the Bondurants who went to
2 CONT Bedford County, Virginia, and later to Kentucky in 1781. His
2 CONT family name remained on the tax list there until 1805. In 1795
2 CONT Martha, John's wife, relinquished her dower in 200 acres of
2 CONT land which her husband sold. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.
2 CONT RICHARD BONDURANT, the second son of John, II, and Sarah
2 CONT Moseley Bondurant was born August 22, 1740, in Manakin Town. He married Cecelia Ann Hall and they had three children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their first born, Thomas, married Margaret Drury and they went to Boone County, Kentucky, in 1820. Frances, their only girl, married Jacob Holsclaw and they too went to Boone County. Their third child was Joseph, who married Marth
2 CONC a Tharp. Joseph and Martha moved westward and one of their sons, Alexander Connelly Bondurant, founded the town of Bondurant, Iowa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Thomas Miles, born in 1744. Died in Buckingham County in 1829.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Darby, born January 1, 1749. Died November 1, 1828.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT  http://www.stithvalley.com/ancestry/bonduran/photocpy.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed mother 
2 CONT
2 CONT Although several online sources say the mother of this family is Rhoda Ann Faure (Ford), the Bonderant Family Association, which has done extensive research on this family says this:
2 CONT "Jean Pierre married Ann Tanner and they had five children: Joseph, John, Ann, Frances, and Peter."
2 CONT https://www.bondurant-family.org/styled-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.bondurant-family.org/styled-21/ BFA Genealogy Research Committee
2 CONT "The Genealogy Research Committee was established by the BFA membership at the October 26, 2019 annual meeting in Portland, Oregon. Its purpose is “to further our understanding of the various Bondurant family lineages descending f
2 CONC rom John Peter (Jean Pierre) Bondurant and Ann Tanner, and assist Members in moving forward in their research so that they can firmly establish their connections to the correct lineage” using traditional genealogical methods as we
2 CONC ll as DNA testing."
2 CONT
2 CONT The one thing everyone seems to agree on is that her name was Ann. The plaque that the family erected in 1990 says "Jean Pierre Bonderant and his wife Ann. ... He married Ann... Their five children are John, Peter, Jospeh, Ann and
2 CONC  Frances." No mention of a birth name for Ann.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also https://www.bondurant-family.org/styled-7/ where it refers to several publications, one of which is The Bondurants of America - Ann Tanner's Ancestors by Mary Bondurant, (Name: Heritage Papers; Location: Athens, Georgia, 
2 CONC USA; Date: 2009;).
2 CONT
2 CONT Geni has Ann Tanner locked on Jean Pierre Bonderant as his wife and the mother of his children.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From Bundrant.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation No. 2
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  JEAN PIERRE2 BONDURANT, JR. (JEAN PIERRE1) was born in Virginia USA.  He married ANN FAURE 1728. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of JEAN BONDURANT and ANN FAURE is:
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.             i.   RICHARD3 BONDURANT, b. 1740.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lawrpaul/bondurant-o/p41.htm#i301
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peter Bondurant [Sr.]
2 CONT
2 CONT #301, b. circa 1710, d. circa 1774
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peter Bondurant [Sr.]|b. c 1710\nd. c 1774|p41.htm#i301|Jean Pierre Bondurant|b. 18 Jul 1677\nd. b 25 Jan 1734/35|p41.htm#i299|Ann Tanner|b. c 1695|p131.htm#i300|Jean P. Bondurant|b. c 1636\nd. 24 May 1694|p41.htm#i343|Gabrie
2 CONC lle Barjon|b. 18 Jan 1643\nd. 23 Mar 1695|p34.htm#i344|Edward Tanner [Sr.]||p131.htm#i68903|Mary Hatcher||p86.htm#i68904|
2 CONT
2 CONT Parent	Jean Pierre Bondurant b. 18 Jul 1677, d. b 25 Jan 1734/35
2 CONT
2 CONT Parent	Ann Tanner b. c 1695
2 CONT
2 CONT Charts	Descendants of Jean Pierre Bondurant
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship	5th great-granduncle of Paul Edward Lawrence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship	Son of Jean Pierre Bondurant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship	29th great-grandson of Charlemagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peter Bondurant [Sr.] was born circa 1710 in King William Parish, Goochland Co., Virginia.1,2 He married Sarah Rachael Moseley about 1729 or 1736.1,2,3 John died circa 1774 in Buckingham Co., Virginia.1,2,4
2 CONT
2 CONT John Peter Bondurant was listed as a vestryman in King William Parish in 1748. He is first mentioned in his father's will in 1734. John and his wife Sarah lived in Goochland County, Virginia, and later in Cumberland County. He dee
2 CONC ded 200 acres of land to his son, John Peter III of Albemarle County, on 9 March 1758.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was the widow of Robert L. Moseley. The Bondurant Family Association Newsletter reprinting information from The Huguenot Magazine, Vol. 25, page 173 gives the marriage date as 1836 but indicates date and place not proved.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grinnell, in his manuscript, indicates that John died in Manakin in 1744. A pedigree chart in The Huguenot, Publication No. 30, submitted by Mary V. Bondurant Epling, indicates that John died about 1744 in Buckingham County, but b
2 CONC efore 1776, and that his death was recorded in Powhatten County. A GEDCOM received from Ruby Talley Smith indicated he died in 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family: Sarah Rachael Taylor
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT *     Jane Bondurant
2 CONT *     *Sarah Rachel Bondurant
2 CONT *     Obediah Bondurant
2 CONT *     Joel Bondurant
2 CONT *     John Bondurant Jr. b. 1737, d. 1810
2 CONT *     Richard Bondurant [Sr.] b. c 1740
2 CONT *     Thomas Miles Bondurant b. c 1744, d. 5 Oct 1829
2 CONT *      Darby Bondurant b. 1 Jan 1749, d. 1 Nov 1828
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations
2 CONT *    1. [S4] The Huguenot Society. The Huguenot 1981-1983. Midlothian, Virginia: The Huguenot Society, the Founders of Manakin in the Colony of Virginia, Inc.).
2 CONT *    2. [S511] The Bondurant Family, compiled by Wiley B. Grinnell, Sr.. 1979. Private Printing, Copy in researcher's file, Fairfield Glade, Tennessee.
2 CONT *    3. [S436] The Bondurant Family Association Newsletter.
2 CONT *    4. [S548] Bondurant Family. 27 August 1998. Copy in researcher's file, Fairfield Glade, Tennessee.
