1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Holman-II/6000000020883068371
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frances Jane Bondurant''' was born as Francoise Jeanne, June 1712 in Manakintowne, Henrico County, Province of Virginia. Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-22910538 Dr. Jean Pierre Bondurant] and his wife [https://w
2 CONC ww.geni.com/profile-59991967 Ann Bondurant]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Before her father's death, she married fellow Huguenot refugee, Pierre/Peter Sallee, in 1733 in Goochland County, as she is named as "Frances Sallee" in her father's 1734 will.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Jane married [https://www.geni.com/profile-52912820 Peter Salle] in 1735 in of Virginia, VA, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-75402557 Isaac Salle]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-38883563 Abraham Salle]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-102055727 Marie Salle]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34636230692 Jacob Bondurant Salle]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34780543436 Joseph Albertus Salle, Sr]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34780543440 Judith Sallee]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in November 1777 in Powhatan County, Virginia, United States and was buried in Cumberland, Cumberland County, Virginia, United States of America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Pierre "John Peter" Bondurant made a will on 25 September 1734. The will of John Peter Bondurant, Goochland County, Virginia: … Item: I give to my daughter '''Francis Sallee''' one heifer at the age of eighteen months and one
2 CONC  sow and pigs to her and her heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed mother
2 CONT Although several online sources say the mother of this family is Rhoda Ann Faure (Ford), the Bonderant Family Association, which has done extensive research on this family says this:
2 CONT "Jean Pierre married Ann Tanner and they had five children: Joseph, John, Ann, Frances, and Peter."
2 CONT https://www.bondurant-family.org/styled-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?o=0&m=612.1.1.1.1.1.2&p=surnames.sallee
2 CONT
2 CONT gleaned mostly from “The Family History of the French Huguenot Abraham Sallé and His Descendants” compiled by Jack Dalton Bailey:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Abraham Sallee – Olive Perrault
2 CONT **2.  1.  Pierre (Peter) – Frances Bondurant (''actually Francoise Jeanne Bondurant'')
2 CONT ***3.  Isaac Sallee (b. 5 Oct 1734) m. 6 May 1759 - Elizabeth Bryant (Brian, Bryan, Briant), d/o James Bryant and Elizabeth LeFevre, d/o Isaac LeFevre
2 CONT **2. 2.  Guillaume (William) Sallee – Elizabeth Givaudan 1st wifeGuillaume (William) Sallee – Magdelaine Chastain 2nd wife
2 CONT ***3.  Isaac Sallee (b. 22 Apr 1741 – Listed in the “Douglas Register")“may” have married ca. 1763 Frances Eden (Eddins?)
2 CONT
2 CONT === Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Françoise Jane (Bondurant) Sallee (1712-1777) who married Jean Pierre Sallee (1705-1752) is connected to the above parents with sources, incl the will that has her married name of Sallee.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT It does ''not'' appear she was also married as below:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Jane married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34645870194 James D Holman, II]. Together they had the following children [https://www.geni.com/profile-34796856644 John Holman]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000194436069844&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Boddie, John Bennett "Mallett and Salle of Manakintown, Va."  Page 144''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
