1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA .  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A011941  DAR Ancestor #: A011941]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/r/a/Jennifer-L-Brazzell/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0706.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Augustine Bondurant was born 1720 in Manakintown, Goochland, Virginia, and died July 30, 1806 in Buckingham, VA. He married Agnes Radford, daughter of John Radford and Elizabeth Maxey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Joseph Augustine Bondurant: Will of Dr. Joseph Bondurant
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Joseph Bondurant was preserved by his descendents in Kentucky. It was dated 26 November 1803 and was proved 11 August 1806, and in it he gave to his daughter, Anne Maxey, one Negro named Sillar. One of the four executo
2 CONC rs he appointed was his son-in-law, Charles Maxey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph Augustine Bondurant and Agnes Radford are:
2 CONT
2 CONT +Anne Bondurant, b. November 10, 1745, Goochland Co., VA, d. 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "The Maxey's of Virginia" p485
2 CONT
2 CONT >Note: the name Suckey was included early in Joseph Bondurant's will amoung slaves going to his wife.  But the repetition of that name in two other places, as reflected [in the notes of William B. Moseley*] , was an error made by 
2 CONC a court clerk in copying from the original will later, where the name Lucy should have appeared.  At the end of the will in two places bondurant named his four daughters as: Ann, Mary, Betty and Lucy.
2 CONT
2 CONT >*notes of William B. Moseley, published in The Huguenot, #24, 1969-71, pp. 122-24)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT @R-894037715@  Ancestry Family Trees  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members. Ancestry Family Tree  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?ti
2 CONC d=87093837&pid=15281
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bondurant Sr. was a son of a Huguenot emigrant (1540-1790).
2 CONT 1776 Project
2 CONT Joseph Bondurant Sr. performed Patriotic Service in Virginia in the American Revolution.
2 CONT Joseph Bondurant, the son of John Peter Bondurant and Ann Tanner was born about 1719 in Henrico, Virginia. He passed away after 26 November 1803 (when he wrote his will) and before 11 August 1806 (when his will was probated).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: It is believed that the original will of Joseph Bondurant is among those lost or destroyed in Buckingham County Records. A copy of the will was preserved by a descendant. The transcript of the will is below is said to be pub
2 CONC lished in the book Genealogical Records of Buckingham County, Virginia, by Whitley, Edythe Johns Rucker. Clearfield Publishing Co. 1984. Pg. 124-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will written in Buckingham County, Virginia, Joseph lists family members: wife, Agnes
2 CONT Son, Joseph
2 CONT Son Edward
2 CONT Son, William
2 CONT Daughter, Ann Maxey 
2 CONT Daughter, Mary Gyers 
2 CONT Daughter, Betty Perkins
2 CONT Daughter, Lucy Landrum
2 CONT
2 CONT He also lists:
2 CONT Slaves by name: Dock, Tom, Daniel, Ben, Sucky, Phyllis and Amy.
2 CONT Executors: Charles Maxey (husband of daughter Ann), Nathan Ayers, Bray Ford, and James Wilson. 
2 CONT Witnesses: Robert Moseley Jr., Daniel Moseley, Thomas Austin and John Hubbard.[1]
2 CONT Will of Joseph Bondurant
2 CONT
2 CONT IN THE NAME OF THE ONLY ETERNAL AND OMNIPOTENT CREATOR, WHO MADE THE WORLD BY THE POWER OF HIS WORD AND GOVERNS THE SAME BY THE UNERRING DICTATES OF HIS WISDOM, I JOSEPH BONDURANT OF BUCKINGHAM COUNTY, BEING OF SOUND AND DISPOSING
2 CONC  MIND AND RECOLLECTION, DO MAKE AND APPOINT THIS WRITING TO BE MY LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT. MY SOUL I CHEERFULLY GIVE UNTO THE MERCIFUL HANDS THAT GAVE IT TO ME, HOPE THIS THE MEDIATION OF MY EVER BLESSED SAVIOUR, THE SAME REMISSIO
2 CONC N OF MY MANIFOLD SINS AND TRANSGRESSIONS WHICH I FREELY GRANT TO ALL THOSE WHO HAVE AT ANY TIME TRANSGRESSED AGAINST ME. MY BODY I WISH TO BE COMMITTED TO I T S KINDRED EARTH, IN SUCH DECENT AND CHRISTIAN LAST MANNER AS TO MY EXEC
2 CONC UTORS SEEM FIT.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE AND CONFIRM TO EACH AND EVERY ONE OF MY CHILDREN, IHE SEVERAL AND RESPECTFULLY AND RESPECTIVELY AS HERETOFORE BESTOWED ON THEM BY ME, AND NOW IN THEIR RESPECTIVE POSSESSIONS, FREE FROM FUTURE DIVISION AND PARTITIONS OF MY E
2 CONC STATE.
2 CONT
2 CONT I RENDER TO MY FAITHFUL AND BELOVED WIFE, AGNES. DURING HER LIFETIME THE LAND AND PLANTATION WHEREON I NOW LIVE. MY NEGROES, DICK, TOM, DANIEL, BEN, SUCKY, PHYLLIS, AND AMY, ALSO STOCK, FURNITURE, AND PLANTATION TOOLS AND UTENSILS
2 CONC  TO HER USE DURING LIFE, AND AT HER DEATH TO BE DIVIDED AS HEREINAFTER DECREED.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE AND CONFIRM TO MY SON, JOSEPH. THE LAND WHERE TO FORE CONVEYED HIM BY DEED.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE TO MY SON, EDWARD. THAT PART OF LAND AND PLANTATION I NOW LIVE ON THAT LIES NORTH OF A DIVIDING LINE THAT I SHALL BEGIN WHERE MOSELEY'S LINE CROSSES THE NORTH FORK OF SLATE RIVER, THENCE DOWN SAID RIVER ONE HUNDRED AND FORT
2 CONC Y THREE POLES CROSSING THE SAME AT A BRIDGE JUST ABOVE THE FORD, AND DOWN THE SAME TO A WHITE OAK SAPLING ON THE BANK, NORTH PORTH-SEVEN DEGREES, EAST 42 POLE TO A SMALL BLACK WALNUT SAPLING, IN THE EDGE OF A ROAD ADJOINING TO BEN
2 CONC JAMIN TINDALL, FROM THENCE ALONG THE «SAID TINDALL'S TO THE LINE OF FRANCIS FORSEE, THENCE ALONG THE SAID FORSEE'S LINE TO THE LINE OF MOSELEY, AND FROK THENCE ALONG THE MOSELEY L I N E TO THE BEGINNING CONTAINING BY SURVEY 220 AC
2 CONC RES, BUT THE SAME MORE OR LESS, TO HIM AND HIS HEIRS FOREVER, BUT NOT TO BE POSSESSED OR ENJOYED TO THE INJURY OF HIS MOTHER DURING HER LIFETIME.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE TO MY SON, WILLIAM. THE REMAINING PART OF THE LAND I LIVE ON, TO HIM AND HIS HEIRS FOREVER, SUBJECT TO THE LIFE RESTRICTIONS DURING HIS MOTHER'S LIFETIME, AS BEFORE MENTIONED TO EDWARD; ALSO TWO NEGROES, TO WIT, SAM AND FRA
2 CONC NK, TO HIM AND HIS HEIRS, FOREVER.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE TO MY DAUGHTER, ANN MAXEY. ONE NEGRO, BY THE NAME OF SILLER, TO HER, AND HER HEIRS, FOREVER.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE TO MY DAUGHTER, MARY AYERS (SIC) , ONE NEGRO GIRL NAMED WINNEY, TO HER AND HER HEIRS FOREVER.
2 CONT
2 CONT I GIVE TO MY DAUGHTER, BETTY PERKINS, ONE NEGRO GIRL NAMED DORCUS, TO HER AND HER HEIRS FOREVER.
2 CONT
2 CONT I LEND THE HIRE AND USE OF MY NEGROES, HANNAH AND JENNY, AND THEIR FUTURE INCREASE TO MY DAUGHTER, LUCY LANDRUM. TO BE ENJOYED BY HER DURING HER LIFETIME AND AT HER DEATH TO BE EQUALLY DIVIDED AMONG HER CHILDREN OR THEIR LEGAL REP
2 CONC RESENTATIVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT IT IS MY WILL THAT SUCH NEGROES I MAY DIE POSSESSED OF AND HAVE NOT BEEN HEREINBEFORE GIVEN AND CONFIRMED TO SOME ONE MEMBER OF MY FAMILY MAY AT MY DEATH BE EQUALLY DIVIDED BETWEEN MY SONS, JOSEPH. EDWARD. WILLIAM. AND MY DAUGHTER
2 CONC S, ANN MAXEY. BETTY. AND LUCY OR THEIR LEGAL REPRESENTATIVES AND THE REST OF MY PROPERTY LENT MY WIPE BE DIVIDED AT HER DEATH AMONG ALL MY CHILDREN OR THEIR LEGAL REPRESENTATIVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT I THINK AN INVENTORY OF MY ESTATE SUFFICIENT AND WISH NO APPRAISEMENT. I CONSTITUTE AND APPOINT MY ESTEEMED FRIENDS, CHARLES MAXEY, NATHAN AYERS (SIC), BRAY FORD AND JAMES WILSON EXECUTORS TO MY LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT, HEREBY REV
2 CONC OKING AND ANNULLING ALL OTHERS HERETOFORE MADE.
2 CONT
2 CONT AS WITNESS MY HAND AND SEAL THIS 26TH. DAY OF NOVEMBER ONE THOUSAND EIGHT HUNDRED AND THREE .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT AT A COURT HELD FOR BUCKINGHAM COUNTY THE 11TH DAY OF AUGUST, 1806 THIS WILL WAS PROVED BY THE OATHS OF ROBERT MOSELEY, JR., DANIEL MOSELEY, AND THOMAS AUSTIN, THREE OF THE WITNESSES THERETO AND SWORN TO BY NATHAN AYERS (SIC) AND 
2 CONC CHARLES MAXEY, TWO OF THE EXECUTORS, WHO ENTERED INTO AND ACKNOWLEDGED BOND WITH SECURITY ACCORDING TO THE LAW CERTIFICATE WAS GRANTED THEM FOR OBTAINING A PROBATE THERE IN DUE FORM.
2 CONT
2 CONT TESTE. ROLFE ELDRIDGE, CLERK. CW COPY TEST. R. ELDRIDGE.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timeline of Records
2 CONT
2 CONT 1737. JOSEPH AUGUSTINE BONDURANT. THE SON OF THE IMMIGRANT, JEAN PIERRE BONDURANT AND ANN FAURE/FORD, FIRST APPEARS ON THE TITHE LIST IN KING WILLIAM PARISH, POWHATAN COUNTY, VA IN 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1743. FROM: HUGUENOT EMIGRATION TO VA. BY BROCK; PAGE 103: APRIL 2 , 1743 : JOSEPH BQNDURAN, GODFATHER FOR GUILLEUM (WILLIAM) LOUCADOW (LOUCADEAU?), SON OF PIERRE LOUCADOW AND ELIZABETH, HIS WIFE.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1749-50. FROM: VIRGINIA MAGAZINE». VOLUME 13 , PAGE 275: VESTRY BOOK OF KING WILLIAM PARISH: (l749) JOSEPH BONDURAN AND JEAN BONDURAN ( HIS BROTHER, TOOK THE OATH OF VESTRYMEN FOR THE PARISH OF KING WILLIAM. THE SAME DAY, JOSEPH B
2 CONC ONDURAN ALSO TOOK THE OATH OF A CHURCHWARDEN FOR THE PRESENT YEAR. (AGAIN IN FEBRUARY, 1750 PAGE 275 .)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1764. LAND PATENT BOOK 35. PAGE 471: JUNE 27.1764: A PATENT FOR 1,400 ACRES OF LAND IN THE COUNTY OF ALBEMARLE I S GRANTED TO JOSEPH BONDURANT (FOR 7 POUNDS) - ON RIPLEY CREEK—THE NORTH BRANCHES OF SLATE RIVER—ADJOINING LANDS OF T
2 CONC HOMAS AND DUBBS—ANTHONY DUBREL—JOHN BONDURANT—ANTHONY BEANING—CAPT. THOMAS BALLON—WILLIAM WALTON, DEC'D—JOHN RIPLEY—THOMAS PATTERSON, ETC. (SIGNED BY FRANCIS FAQUIER, ESQ.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1770. DEED BOOK NO. 4, PAGE 410: JOSEPH BONDURANT. OF THE PARISH OF KING WILLIAM, COUNTY OF CUMBERLAND, SELLS TO RICHARD JAMES, OF THE SAME COUNTY, FOR 175 POUNDS...A TRACT OF LAND IN SAID COUNTY WHEREON THE SAID BONDURANT NOW LIV
2 CONC ES, ON BONDURANT BRANCH... JONES CREEK, ADJOINING LANDS OF THOMAS TURPIN...CONTAINING 125 ACRES OF LAND, ETC. ACKNOWLEDGED BY JOSEPH BONDURANT: JUNE 25, 1770: (CUMBERLAND CO. V A . DECEMBER 29, 1768.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1772. RECORDED: CUMBERLAND CO. DEED BOOK 5, PAGE 189: SEPTEMBER 28, 1772: JOSEPH BONDURANT AND AGNES. HIS WIFE, OF CUMBERLAND COUNTY, SELL TO SAMUEL FLOURNOY, OF THE SAME COUNTY, FOR $230... A TRACT OF LAND IN SAID COUNTY WHEREON 
2 CONC THE SAID JOSEPH BONDURANT NOW LIVES, ON THE WEST SIDE OF JONES CREEK, ETC., CONTAINING 125 ACRES, ETC. WITNESSES: JOHN RADFORD. JANE RADFORD, WILLIAM WILSON (OR WATSON) NOTE: OF THESE TWO TRACTS OF LAND, ONE HE INHERITED FROM HIS 
2 CONC FATHER IN 1735, AND THE OTHER WAS DEED OF GIFT FROM HIS FATHER-IN- LAW, JOHN RADFORD. I N 1747. (SEE DEED) THIS WOULD LEAVE HIM THE 1,400 ACRES OF LAND HE PATENTED IN 1764 AND WHICH UNDOUBTEDLY LATER FELL IN BUCKINGHAM COUNTY WHEN
2 CONC  THAT COUNTY WAS FORMED.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1782 VIRGINIA TAX RECORDS: BUCKINGHAM COUNTY. 1782 . WHITES: JOHN BONDURANT Blacks - 1 JOSEPH BONDURANT, SR. Blacks-21 JOSEPH BONDURANT, JR. Blacks-1 THOMAS BONDURANT DARBY BONDURANT Blacks-1 OBEDIAH BONDURANT.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1806. NEWSPAPER! THE ARGUS. EDITION OF AUGUST I6TH, I806: PAGE 3, LAST COLUMN: JOSEPH BONDURANT.. ."DEPARTED THIS LIFE ON THE 30TH JULY LAST, (1806) DR. JOSEPH BONDURANT. I N HIS 87TH. YEAR. * THUS BORN IN 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1830. SUIT IN CHANCERY: OCTOBER 20, 1830: POWHATAN COUNTY ORDER BOOK 21 . PAGE 331: DEFENDANTS: ( FORMERLY BONDURANTS:) ANN MAXEY, FORMERLY ANN BONDURANT, WIFE OF CHARLES MAXEY, ELIZABETH APPERSON, FORMERLY ELIZABETH BONDURANT (JO
2 CONC HN APPERSON) (EPPERSON), LUCY DAVIS, FORMERLY LUCY BONDURANT (JEFFREY DAVIS), JOSEPH BONDURANT, EDWARD BONDURANT, WILLIAM BONDURANT, MARY AYRES, NATHAN AYRES
2 CONT
2 CONT ALL CERTIFIED IN THE CITED RECORD AS THE CHILDREN OF AGNES BONDURANT, DEC'D, WHO WAS FORMERLY AGNES RADFORD:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1781. PUBLIC SERVICE CLAIMS; AUGUST 15. 1781; ORIGINAL CERTIFICATE AS ISSUED: "RECEIVED OF JOSEPH BONDURANT, OF BUCKINGHAM COUNTY, VIRGINIA, 625 LBS. OF GRASS FED BEEF, AT TWO PENCE PER,. .SPECIE IS 5 POUNDS, 4 SHILLINGS, AND 2 PE
2 CONC NCE. SIGNED BY THOMAS ANDERSON:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1780. VIRGINIA MAGAZINE: VOLUME NO. 2, PAGE 206: POWHATAN COUNTY WILL BOOK NO. 1, PAGE 66: WILL OF SAMUEL FLOURNOY, SON OF JEAN JACQUES FLOURNOY, DATED: SEPTEMBER, I78O: PROVED: DECEMBER 21, 1780: HE LEAVES 475 ACRES OF LAND TO HI
2 CONC S SON, GIDEON FLOURNOY, WHICH IS LAND HE PURCHASED FROM JOSEPH BONDURANT.. .JOHN RADFORD AND RICHARD EPPERSON.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Unless there is a source that Joseph graduated from a medical school and was awarded a degree in medicine, "MD" should not be used. Given the day and time, he most likely learned to be a doctor from his father. That doesn't make h
2 CONC im an MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Note: {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA . [https:/services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb?action=full&p_id=A011941 DAR Ancestor #: A011941].
2 CONT
2 CONT >Note: the name Suckey was included early in Joseph Bondurant's will among slaves going to his wife. But the repetition of that name in two other places, as reflected [in the notes of William B. Moseley*] , was an error made by a 
2 CONC court clerk in copying from the original will later, where the name Lucy should have appeared. At the end of the will in two places bondurant named his four daughters as: Ann, Mary, Betty and Lucy.[3]
2 CONT
