1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Baptiste_Louis_Andrault '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch====
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Baptiste_Louis_Andrault_de_Maul%C3%A9vrier English - '''Wikipedia....'''], [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Baptiste_Louis_Andrault Français - '''Wikipedia....''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean-Baptiste Louis Andrault de Maulévrier From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean-Baptiste Louis Andrault, marquis de Maulévrier (November 3, 1677 – March 20, 1754) was a French military and diplomat.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as aide de camp of Marshal Nicolas Catinat in Italy. He became brigadier in 1704, lieutenant general in 1720 and Marshal of France in 1745. He was also ambassadeur extraordinaire for the French King at the Spanish court 
2 CONC in 1720, where he '''received the Order of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Charles Claude Andrault de Langeron (1720–1792), became also a lieutenant general in the King's Army.
